Securing API endpoints involves implementing measures like:
- Using OAuth for authentication
- Implementing rate limiting and IP blocking
- Enabling API keys for additional security

For example, using OAuth:
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const passport = require('passport');

app.use(express.json());
app.use(passport.initialize());
app.use(passport.session());

// API endpoint with OAuth authentication
app.get('/api/endpoint', passport.authenticate('jwt'), (req, res) => {
  // Process request and return response
});
```
